<h1>hyperedge</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A connection between any number of <a href="vertex.html"><em>vertices</em></a> of a  <a href="hypergraph.html"><em>hypergraph</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Formal Definition:</strong> A hyperedge is a <a href="set.html"><em>set</em></a> of vertices of a hypergraph.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Aggregate parent</strong> (I am a part of or used in ...)<br>
<a href="hypergraph.html"><em>hypergraph</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="edge.html"><em>edge</em></a>, <a href="graph.html"><em>graph</em></a>, <a href="directedGraph.html"><em>directed graph</em></a>, <a href="undirectedGraph.html"><em>undirected graph</em></a>, <a href="weightedGraph.html"><em>weighted graph</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

